<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Virupaksha Temple, Pattadakal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Virupaksha Temple at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pattadakal">Pattadakal</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> temple dedicated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiva">Shiva</a>, built around 740 by Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lokamahadevi">Lokamahadevi</a> to commemorate the victory of her husband, the Chalukya king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikramaditya-ii">Vikramaditya II</a>, over the Pallavas. Modelled partly on the Kailasanatha temple at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanchipuram">Kanchipuram</a>, it is a masterpiece of early Dravidian architecture and part of the Pattadakal World Heritage Site.</p></div>
